lue "A hyperbola with semiaxes $\\sqrt{3}$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94997/selection/d7220d749a75d6a1bb8298be75144fe102af6b6fa029454a3bdfc3fcbfbb0174" :answer/id #uuid "1b925199-c569-5d41-ad1a-b87d9b7e6c4f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A hyperbola with semiaxes $3$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94997/selection/760e48720bc1f040f55d664d7d077f6360f65d53d04715776978232d40e278ba" :answer/id #uuid "8351a868-05fc-5924-82b5-3ba01988d0c6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An ellipse with semiaxes $1$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94997/selection/97302f3e21cc609c6d785f09d9b0370e8423f3b9291de0d2837d09625aadb1f0" :answer/id #uuid "3cd6d3de-6aa3-59d5-b032-24a30d24dda9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A circle of radius $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94997/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "51919194-e46e-5335-925b-d37134beb834" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94997/selection/58644f6f0dc2d0ea3af8a86a1346fac0b2172dd2cfaed0549f78787575df57b2" :answer-field/choices ["q-94997/selection/58644f6f0dc2d0ea3af8a86a1346fac0b2172dd2cfaed0549f78787575df57b2" "q-94997/selection/f3c0ff97de2ddec575a035305b646da219e63ac237464f7a9437846b5ffca998" "q-94997/selection/d7220d749a75d6a1bb8298be75144fe102af6b6fa029454a3bdfc3fcbfbb0174" "q-94997/selection/760e48720bc1f040f55d664d7d077f6360f65d53d04715776978232d40e278ba" "q-94997/selection/97302f3e21cc609c6d785f09d9b0370e8423f3b9291de0d2837d09625aadb1f0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94997" :question/id #uuid "524143ac-0f98-5858-ae7f-d1be1f96a542" :question/math-academy-id "q-94997" :question/problem "Which curve is defined by the equation $5{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+5{x}_{2}^{2}=12?$" :question/worked-solution "Consider the quadratic form $Q(x)=5{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+5{x}_{2}^{2}.$ To determine the curve defined by the given equation, we reduce $Q(x)$ to its canonical (diagonal) form.\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of $Q(x),$ which is\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNext, we find the eigenvalues of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +24 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =6,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our quadratic form can be reduced to $6{y}_{1}^{2}+4{y}_{2}^{2}.$ \n\nIn the new variables, the curve has the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{y}_{1}^{2}+4{y}_{2}^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}+\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is an ellipse with semiaxes $\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\sqrt{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94997/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5d6ac06-40b4-5da0-bd26-860b35826292"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94997"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140549/selection/9435b0e6b96b139c9a5d039f54b09b5ff5ee8555305a9785518a5505f9f17148" :answer/id #uuid "aca36349-4f7f-536a-a6bd-a34442139674" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Two parallel lines" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140549/selection/f458f5c3c87a9b27674e3c0a35b35da19f1861a95816d21e65a646f1b9997edc" :answer/id #uuid "499b271e-9581-5e77-9938-e2f3f220eb64" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A hyperbola with semiaxes $6$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140549/selection/25d0f49d13d874fa89da254ee3edc8aa69da6439b17a56fb39af3a5e7dcbff7d" :answer/id #uuid "50a727c0-0c69-5cde-bd49-a23ec0c6563f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An ellipse with semiaxes $\\sqrt{6}$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140549/selection/c56c8beee168edd136b2839bdcacd192692e1e98daffcb8ee93b14a613acaff9" :answer/id #uuid "757b6751-ea84-5cfc-8e9e-651cd3229119" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An ellipse with semiaxes $6$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140549/selection/90b7f0a12ee911e05ad2bc8de85e1c5f3850fc3294e42b5062c8bb5212ac07e5" :answer/id #uuid "6c994f35-b46d-5c1c-93e7-2ac8178cae09" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A hyperbola with semiaxes $\\sqrt{6}$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140549/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8df24f14-2ef2-533c-908d-480d4f782c93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140549/selection/90b7f0a12ee911e05ad2bc8de85e1c5f3850fc3294e42b5062c8bb5212ac07e5" :answer-field/choices ["q-140549/selection/9435b0e6b96b139c9a5d039f54b09b5ff5ee8555305a9785518a5505f9f17148" "q-140549/selection/f458f5c3c87a9b27674e3c0a35b35da19f1861a95816d21e65a646f1b9997edc" "q-140549/selection/25d0f49d13d874fa89da254ee3edc8aa69da6439b17a56fb39af3a5e7dcbff7d" "q-140549/selection/c56c8beee168edd136b2839bdcacd192692e1e98daffcb8ee93b14a613acaff9" "q-140549/selection/90b7f0a12ee911e05ad2bc8de85e1c5f3850fc3294e42b5062c8bb5212ac07e5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140549" :question/id #uuid "042ead02-bb3a-5e4c-9374-7ae765cba5f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-140549" :question/problem "Which curve is defined by the equation $3{x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2}=24?$" :question/worked-solution "Consider the quadratic form $Q(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2}.$ To determine the curve defined by the given equation, we reduce $Q(x)$ to its canonical (diagonal) form.\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of $Q(x),$ which is\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNext, we find the eigenvalues of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & -3 \\\\ -3 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -24 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =4,\\,-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our quadratic form can be reduced to $4{y}_{1}^{2}-6{y}_{2}^{2}.$ \n\nIn the new variables, the curve has the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}_{1}^{2}-6{y}_{2}^{2} & =24 \\\\ \\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{6})^{2}}-\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a hyperbola with semiaxes $\\sqrt{6}$ and $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-140549/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5d6ac06-40b4-5da0-bd26-860b35826292"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140549"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95015/selection/9435b0e6b96b139c9a5d039f54b09b5ff5ee8555305a9785518a5505f9f17148" :answer/id #uuid "4d0cb43e-a7c0-5d13-b2f1-36f4a84cb03e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Two parallel lines" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95015/selection/d8647bcc9e9a6500f48c3b93b8b307edaa5fc3a9c63f31c5cfc0f1db454b73ae" :answer/id #uuid "5676c7ce-c404-584d-914a-54f047309b02" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An ellipse with semiaxes $3$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95015/selection/c80eeadc3d84002f1ac6b8d11b525c7a30a17f83e1f2a4e7a35896dd75338a9b" :answer/id #uuid "8400b830-3a4b-5b22-8b86-72f5fc69dba4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A hyperbola with semiaxes $\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95015/selection/390b53390d141b05e8521d71bcf5423e2d7b2df4bc22b5b5cd9cc26b97ee2338" :answer/id #uuid "a3ee7e10-e9c1-5269-b207-c0ec980965d5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A hyperbola with semiaxes $3$ and $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95015/selection/b074ce4ee1a49a5e3fbd388d3ff728d609e012c6139173fe235a56bf6734f883" :answer/id #uuid "f7309976-06df-5972-9f81-e69407786d0b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A circle with radius $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95015/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b8c34c9b-2fd8-5c84-b0b7-43c46106e09f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95015/selection/c80eeadc3d84002f1ac6b8d11b525c7a30a17f83e1f2a4e7a35896dd75338a9b" :answer-field/choices ["q-95015/selection/9435b0e6b96b139c9a5d039f54b09b5ff5ee8555305a9785518a5505f9f17148" "q-95015/selection/d8647bcc9e9a6500f48c3b93b8b307edaa5fc3a9c63f31c5cfc0f1db454b73ae" "q-95015/selection/c80eeadc3d84002f1ac6b8d11b525c7a30a17f83e1f2a4e7a35896dd75338a9b" "q-95015/selection/390b53390d141b05e8521d71bcf5423e2d7b2df4bc22b5b5cd9cc26b97ee2338" "q-95015/selection/b074ce4ee1a49a5e3fbd388d3ff728d609e012c6139173fe235a56bf6734f883"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95015" :question/id #uuid "2b7fa421-8274-5a15-90a7-f07c79709eb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-95015" :question/problem "Which curve is defined by the equation $-5{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}=12?$" :question/worked-solution "Consider the quadratic form $Q(x)=-5{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}.$ To determine the curve defined by the given equation, we reduce $Q(x)$ to its canonical (diagonal) form.\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of $Q(x),$ which is\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNext, we find the eigenvalues of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-5-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -24 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =4,\\,-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our quadratic form can be reduced to $4{y}_{1}^{2}-6{y}_{2}^{2}.$ \n\nIn the new variables, the curve has the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}_{1}^{2}-6{y}_{2}^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}}-\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a hyperbola with semiaxes $\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95015/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5d6ac06-40b4-5da0-bd26-860b35826292"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95015"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95000/selection/a204822af26fdd8e45f7b71277e5e1af2353776ab5592eb217541933aeecbc0b" :answer/id #uuid "7375a74b-35c8-5078-82e7-cc4d5e1be5db" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A circle with radius $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95000/selection/e8fcc5237b6bbc36e2ab7afd24afa6e2ba397d1327cad48d98ab9d9cd40f80de" :answer/id #uuid "7ff76bb0-e0a4-5f53-85a7-7bc7089dc663" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A hyperbola with semiaxes $\\sqrt{2}$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95000/selection/20f059a38e10af09c6a26b6ec33dfbd2d98b44d5907c43400a34bff58081a571" :answer/id #uuid "8e38b7ce-bd28-5611-984c-3d2523813823" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An ellipse with semiaxes $-1$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95000/selection/756caf8fd3453ecaae1240d575da1d4bbd085d792cd0fa784450aba51f8d776e" :answer/id #uuid "c4c774e2-7fae-53ab-b632-2dbef3a59556" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A pair of intersecting lines" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95000/selection/b06ed78f6dedc9653a9d972584a4a52b65f74795851da280e18b865394af8035" :answer/id #uuid "68eac365-a32d-5074-bffc-d572275570ee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A parabola" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95000/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6ea237b0-048f-539e-b0c4-52571eb82fe0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95000/selection/e8fcc5237b6bbc36e2ab7afd24afa6e2ba397d1327cad48d98ab9d9cd40f80de" :answer-field/choices ["q-95000/selection/a204822af26fdd8e45f7b71277e5e1af2353776ab5592eb217541933aeecbc0b" "q-95000/selection/e8fcc5237b6bbc36e2ab7afd24afa6e2ba397d1327cad48d98ab9d9cd40f80de" "q-95000/selection/20f059a38e10af09c6a26b6ec33dfbd2d98b44d5907c43400a34bff58081a571" "q-95000/selection/756caf8fd3453ecaae1240d575da1d4bbd085d792cd0fa784450aba51f8d776e" "q-95000/selection/b06ed78f6dedc9653a9d972584a4a52b65f74795851da280e18b865394af8035"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95000" :question/id #uuid "749c0e99-8e51-5cee-8388-727f4d22f48f" :question/math-academy-id "q-95000" :question/problem "Which curve is defined by the equation ${x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=8?$" :question/worked-solution "Consider the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}.$ To determine the curve defined by the given equation, we reduce $Q(x)$ to its canonical (diagonal) form.\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of $Q(x),$ which is\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNext, we find the eigenvalues of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -8 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =4,\\,-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our quadratic form can be reduced to $4{y}_{1}^{2}-2{y}_{2}^{2}.$ \n\nIn the new variables, the curve has the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}_{1}^{2}-2{y}_{2}^{2} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}-\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a hyperbola with semiaxes $\\sqrt{2}$ and $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95000/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5d6ac06-40b4-5da0-bd26-860b35826292"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95000"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-94596"] :question/problem "Which curve is defined by the equation $2{x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+10{x}_{2}^{2}=44?$" :question/worked-solution "Consider the quadratic form $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+10{x}_{2}^{2}.$ To determine the curve defined by the given equation, we reduce $Q(x)$ to its canonical (diagonal) form.\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of $Q(x),$ which is\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNext, we find the eigenvalues of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & -3 \\\\ -3 & 10-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-12\\lambda +11 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =11,\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our quadratic form can be reduced to $11{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}.$ \n\nIn the new variables, the curve has the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2} & =44 \\\\ \\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{44} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}_{1}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}_{2}^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{11})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is an ellipse with semiaxes $2$ and $2\\sqrt{11}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-97992/selection/0d886085183df1a260e428d1bf8f690275217f82e75e86d5e87f88eebd8a758f" :answer/id #uuid "8aa79f64-b1f9-5610-95b6-f8ea4874729b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97992/selection/1dba8fb74f34098a929725a41b1bd97e6dd7deba82110b280bbfa0162a237080" :answer/id #uuid "716d146d-7c5a-5fdc-a578-baeffb2061fb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97992/selection/9946a6591a484bfd820474c755ab3073410cd966f4d790c250ee7fd8bec9ac67" :answer/id #uuid "20791541-d42c-5701-8c8e-845582b4263f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97992/selection/53c8157735a0f628e9148bc025416a5eabe8dcc83936c698feac58cb630cb595" :answer/id #uuid "4fb78adf-21cf-5c54-a56a-39998bdd78da" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97992/selection/6403e114a237113d976f9a4fc93d769e99ad74091bd0fced0902a9567128ae1f" :answer/id #uuid "9f2d2304-9e8c-5dde-a2f8-e219e077476e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97992/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c93d706d-29b8-5548-9718-1e7d31668399" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97992/selection/0d886085183df1a260e428d1bf8f690275217f82e75e86d5e87f88eebd8a758f" :answer-field/choices ["q-97992/selection/0d886085183df1a260e428d1bf8f690275217f82e75e86d5e87f88eebd8a758f" "q-97992/selection/1dba8fb74f34098a929725a41b1bd97e6dd7deba82110b280bbfa0162a237080" "q-97992/selection/9946a6591a484bfd820474c755ab3073410cd966f4d790c250ee7fd8bec9ac67" "q-97992/selection/53c8157735a0f628e9148bc025416a5eabe8dcc83936c698feac58cb630cb595" "q-97992/selection/6403e114a237113d976f9a4fc93d769e99ad74091bd0fced0902a9567128ae1f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97992" :question/id #uuid "61a6fc08-cff1-54fa-821d-2b21fbaaba50" :question/math-academy-id "q-97992" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]$ and the quadratic curve ${x}^{T}\\,Ax=3.$ Given that $A$ has eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=6$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-4,$ find the principal axes of the curve." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is symmetric. \nThe principal axes of the curve \n\n$$\n{x}^{T}\\,Ax=3\n$$\n\nare the vectors that give an orthonormal eigenvector basis for $A.$ Let's now find these eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-6I & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]-6[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-6I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ Dividing ${v}_{1}$ by its norm $‖{v}_{1}‖=\\sqrt{10},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-4)I & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]+4[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-(-4)I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Dividing ${v}_{2}$ by its norm $‖{v}_{2}‖=\\sqrt{10},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the principal axes of our curve are\n\n$\\,$ $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97992/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e97b8e36-3790-5cdc-bd77-417574af23f3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97992"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97990/selection/e8ae4dc235b5d2d0d8ebec0cfa30042de8990395f5022314446a4061e6a1b13e" :answer/id #uuid "77c371a6-5239-5a4b-a79c-ee4218709a94" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97990/selection/ca1a76cc195e72416a6a17c3721a82bd57e3e6fcc252d58bbb64913f2261c0fe" :answer/id #uuid "1f3472a5-dea0-563e-a3ab-bb20e0af66a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97990/selection/aac5c6cedde568a86c238aa6a9e1a5aa8f28520fc3995d957496ff6c29fcb1d7" :answer/id #uuid "c89635a0-0f12-5653-a3f9-a4ccaca4b53b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97990/selection/3aef26a7d7216a4abc0582bc748d56d2e1ac2768969e5d0bbe2a73a7d9dab378" :answer/id #uuid "400eb914-217f-5405-917b-8d6d946ec880" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97990/selection/9946a6591a484bfd820474c755ab3073410cd966f4d790c250ee7fd8bec9ac67" :answer/id #uuid "9b7ef421-b702-538d-9d34-6cd21eb503b9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97990/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ce6ada2-20d0-5257-ae5c-8dd02ece0b85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97990/selection/9946a6591a484bfd820474c755ab3073410cd966f4d790c250ee7fd8bec9ac67" :answer-field/choices ["q-97990/selection/e8ae4dc235b5d2d0d8ebec0cfa30042de8990395f5022314446a4061e6a1b13e" "q-97990/selection/ca1a76cc195e72416a6a17c3721a82bd57e3e6fcc252d58bbb64913f2261c0fe" "q-97990/selection/aac5c6cedde568a86c238aa6a9e1a5aa8f28520fc3995d957496ff6c29fcb1d7" "q-97990/selection/3aef26a7d7216a4abc0582bc748d56d2e1ac2768969e5d0bbe2a73a7d9dab378" "q-97990/selection/9946a6591a484bfd820474c755ab3073410cd966f4d790c250ee7fd8bec9ac67"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97990" :question/id #uuid "5fb95d9e-0ced-5515-baa2-9595c0717556" :question/math-academy-id "q-97990" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and the quadratic curve ${x}^{T}\\,Ax=7.$ Given that $A$ has eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3,$ find the principal axes of the curve." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is symmetric. \nThe principal axes of the curve \n\n$$\n{x}^{T}\\,Ax=7\n$$\n\nare the vectors that give an orthonormal eigenvector basis for $A.$ Let's now find these eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-2I & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-2I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Dividing ${v}_{1}$ by its norm $‖{v}_{1}‖=\\sqrt{5},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-3)I & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-(-3)I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Dividing ${v}_{2}$ by its norm $‖{v}_{2}‖=\\sqrt{5},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the principal axes of our curve are\n\n$\\,$ $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97990/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e97b8e36-3790-5cdc-bd77-417574af23f3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97990"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97988/selection/d8e04e3f7a4e9194cb31e7f33e4159f3718896e65d07d82d2b6fd0a9756491f5" :answer/id #uuid "6d1e733a-2c19-5f3d-9098-9092978a7d91" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97988/selection/3fa015bdfee9b3575d08a84900a8e5e286c385b1d4ac7b96e7c5418ca399cdcd" :answer/id #uuid "83d3d754-4357-50e6-b7fc-6b21cebc59d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97988/selection/2c8dd2717b4b539cf3fd995c4237442e1fcd1094d45c8172682cf61c8e4e46de" :answer/id #uuid "1f56209b-e044-532c-aeda-543574ca20de" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97988/selection/0a3bb3cecefe0c093108a1db4622b742c4e381272e360deb2694432b7bd90d07" :answer/id #uuid "867c17e6-cfae-582d-b5f0-90f978d62307" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97988/selection/2c139974f94834987dd50ebeb5a6f6dfae83d917cb8cc691c5105086fbba23df" :answer/id #uuid "ffd0be3d-db64-5c4c-8eb1-7d96a2508060" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97988/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bc22569a-e1a1-5369-b389-2256bf925a0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97988/selection/2c8dd2717b4b539cf3fd995c4237442e1fcd1094d45c8172682cf61c8e4e46de" :answer-field/choices ["q-97988/selection/d8e04e3f7a4e9194cb31e7f33e4159f3718896e65d07d82d2b6fd0a9756491f5" "q-97988/selection/3fa015bdfee9b3575d08a84900a8e5e286c385b1d4ac7b96e7c5418ca399cdcd" "q-97988/selection/2c8dd2717b4b539cf3fd995c4237442e1fcd1094d45c8172682cf61c8e4e46de" "q-97988/selection/0a3bb3cecefe0c093108a1db4622b742c4e381272e360deb2694432b7bd90d07" "q-97988/selection/2c139974f94834987dd50ebeb5a6f6dfae83d917cb8cc691c5105086fbba23df"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97988" :question/id #uuid "334c09b2-8068-5ab6-b14b-135919cc8d1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-97988" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]$ and the quadratic curve ${x}^{T}\\,Ax=2.$ Given that $A$ has eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=6$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=4,$ find the principal axes of the curve." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is symmetric. \nThe principal axes of the curve \n\n$$\n{x}^{T}\\,Ax=2\n$$\n\nare the vectors that give an orthonormal eigenvector basis for $A.$ Let's now find these eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-6I & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]-6[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-6I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Dividing ${v}_{2}$ by its norm $‖{v}_{2}‖=\\sqrt{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-4I & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-4I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Dividing ${v}_{1}$ by its norm $‖{v}_{1}‖=\\sqrt{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the principal axes of our curve are\n\n$\\,$ $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97988/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e97b8e36-3790-5cdc-bd77-417574af23f3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97988"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97995/selection/2c8dd2717b4b539cf3fd995c4237442e1fcd1094d45c8172682cf61c8e4e46de" :answer/id #uuid "450361ef-495d-5fa8-a436-c2b9522e261b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97995/selection/c00cf52e39054b9b2a40b5aac29e88cc15953defb404ef0a6003237fd552be9b" :answer/id #uuid "0043eda4-8d36-5567-86fe-0419ffc3d3db" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97995/selection/c4ca8b4a1cfe1c09eb718471b7b6872c13c81218297d86cd18d0ea5e3e46f700" :answer/id #uuid "a1be5595